Prometheus keeps local persistent storage.
So if Thanos/S3 becomes temporarily unavailable:

Prometheus can continue retaining local data
Later, Thanos will upload blocks to S3 once connectivity is available.

Application
    │
    ▼
   Alloy
    │
    ▼
Prometheus
    │
    ├── Local WAL/PVC
    │
    └── Thanos Sidecar ──X── S3 temporarily unavailable


Make sure you are on Monitoring EKS:

kubectl config use-context monitoring-eks

Verify the EBS CSI driver:
=========================
kubectl get pods -n kube-system \
  -l app.kubernetes.io/name=aws-ebs-csi-driver

kubectl get storageclass

the abhove command will show gp2 alone, but we need to create disk as gp3

Create a dedicated gp3 StorageClass:
===================================
cat > monitoring-gp3-storageclass.yaml <<'EOF'
apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1
kind: StorageClass
metadata:
  name: monitoring-gp3
provisioner: ebs.csi.aws.com
volumeBindingMode: WaitForFirstConsumer
allowVolumeExpansion: true
parameters:
  type: gp3
  fsType: ext4
EOF


kubectl apply -f monitoring-gp3-storageclass.yaml

$ kubectl get storageclass
NAME             PROVISIONER             RECLAIMPOLICY   VOLUMEBINDINGMODE      ALLOWVOLUMEEXPANSION   AGE
gp2              kubernetes.io/aws-ebs   Delete          WaitForFirstConsumer   false                  169m
monitoring-gp3   ebs.csi.aws.com         Delete          WaitForFirstConsumer   true                   19s


Add the Prometheus Helm repository:
==================================
helm repo add prometheus-community \
  https://prometheus-community.github.io/helm-charts


$ helm repo update

$ helm search repo prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack
NAME                                            CHART VERSION   APP VERSION     DESCRIPTION
prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack      89.2.2          v0.93.1         kube-prometheus-stack collects Kubernetes manif...



Create Prometheus configuration:
================================

cat > prometheus-values.yaml <<'EOF'
prometheus:
  enabled: true

  prometheusSpec:

    replicas: 2

    replicaExternalLabelName: prometheus_replica

    externalLabels:
      cluster: monitoring-eks
      environment: demo

    retention: 24h

    retentionSize: "40GB"

    walCompression: true

    enableRemoteWriteReceiver: true

    storageSpec:
      volumeClaimTemplate:
        spec:
          storageClassName: monitoring-gp3
          accessModes:
            - ReadWriteOnce
          resources:
            requests:
              storage: 50Gi

    resources:
      requests:
        cpu: 500m
        memory: 2Gi
      limits:
        cpu: "2"
        memory: 4Gi

grafana:
  enabled: false

alertmanager:
  enabled: false

kube-state-metrics:
  enabled: true

prometheus-node-exporter:
  enabled: true

defaultRules:
  create: true
EOF



Install kube-prometheus-stack:
=============================

helm upgrade --install kube-prometheus-stack \
  prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack \
  --namespace monitoring \
  --create-namespace \
  --values prometheus-values.yaml

